content:
Looking at the evidence, I need to understand why I1_payment_has_order still has 39 violations after multiple `replay_payment_confirmations` runs. The replays confirmed hundreds of payments (199+348+94+88=729 total), yet 39 violations persist. I need to check whether these are genuinely unmatched payments (no order exists) vs. orders that exist but aren't confirmed, and whether the invoice-agent v1.1 deploy (E14) is still producing bad data.

```json
{
  "investigate": [
    {
      "tool": "sql",
      "query": "SELECT p.id, p.order_id, p.status, p.created_at, o.id AS order_id_found, o.status AS order_status FROM payments p LEFT JOIN orders o ON o.id = p.order_id WHERE p.status = 'captured' AND (o.id IS NULL OR o.status != 'confirmed') ORDER BY p.created_at DESC LIMIT 50",
      "why": "Identify whether the 39 violations are payments with no matching order row at all, or payments whose order exists but is not yet confirmed — this separates a bad_input/bad_deploy cause from a processing lag."
    },
    {
      "tool": "sql",
      "query": "SELECT p.order_id, p.created_at AS payment_at, o.created_at AS order_created_at, o.status, i.order_id AS invoice_exists FROM payments p LEFT JOIN orders o ON o.id = p.order_id LEFT JOIN invoices i ON i.order_id = p.order_id WHERE p.status = 'captured' AND (o.id IS NULL OR o.status != 'confirmed') ORDER BY p.created_at DESC LIMIT 50",
      "why": "Check whether invoices exist for these orphaned payments — if invoices are missing it points to invoice-agent v1.1 producing orders without invoices; if invoices exist but orders aren't confirmed it points to a workflow/queue processing gap."
    }
  ],
  "hypotheses": [],
  "summary": "Investigating 39 persistent I1 violations to determine whether they are payments with no order, orders stuck unconfirmed, or a structural data problem introduced by the invoice-agent v1.1 deploy."
}
```
